<title>GREECE: CITIBANK, ATHENS RAISES BASE LOAN RATES.</title>
<headline>CITIBANK, ATHENS RAISES BASE LOAN RATES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citibank will raise its base</p>
<p>lending rates for working capital loans and freely investible</p>
<p>funds by 75 basis points for a week effective Tuesday July 22,</p>
<p>it said.</p>
<p>It will also raise its business &amp; professional base lending</p>
<p>rate by 50 basis points, keeping all other base lending rates</p>
<p>unchanged.</p>
<p>Citibank, which reviews its rates weekly, offers the</p>
<p>following lending rate structure:</p>
<p>** Base rate for working capital loans at 16.50 percent</p>
<p>(from 15.75 percent)</p>
<p>** Business and professional base lending rate at 16.75 percent</p>
<p>(from 16.00 percent)</p>
<p>** Base rate for freely investible funds at 16.75 percent</p>
<p>(from 16.25 percent)</p>
<p>** Mortgage rates*:</p>
<p>insurance cost included 14.50 percent</p>
<p>insurance cost not included 14.00 percent</p>
<p>without prenotice 16.00 percent</p>
<p>* customers participating in the New Banking Relationship</p>
<p>are entitled to a 1.0 percent cut in all mortgage rates</p>
<p>** Auto loans through representative at 18.00 percent</p>
<p>** Home improvement loans at 19.75 percent</p>
<p>** Branch auto loans at 19.00 percent</p>
<p>** Personal installment loans steady at 19.50 percent</p>
<p>** Personal installment loans with invoices at 17.00 percent</p>
<p>** Citi-Credit at 21.00 percent</p>
<p>Contribution under Law 128 is not included in the rates</p>
<p>quoted, it said.</p>
<p>Base rates on working capital loans in foreign currency for</p>
<p>this week will be:</p>
<p>    US Dollars     :  8.22 percent</p>
<p>    Marks	    :  5.64 percent</p>
<p>    Yen		:  3.18 percent</p>
<p>    Guilders	 :  5.77 percent</p>
<p>    Ecu		:  6.70 percent</p>
<p>Pounds Sterling:  9.53 percent</p>
<p>French francs  :  5.87 percent</p>
<p>    Swiss francs   :  4.22 percent</p>
<p>Belgian francs :  6.07 percent</p>
<p>    Italian lira   :  9.44 percent</p>
<p>--Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
